<article class="env-definition" id="0G3T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G3T">Definition <span data-tag="0G3T">17.29.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$ be a map of sheaves of rings on $X$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_2$-modules. The module $\mathcal{P}^ k_{\mathcal{O}_2/\mathcal{O}_1}(\mathcal{F})$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0G3S" data-tag="0G3S">17.29.3</a> is called the <em>module of principal parts of order $k$</em> of $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article>